WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.658
Work on one habit at a

2
00:00:02.658 --> 00:00:04.965
time, not all thirteen at once.

3
00:00:06.215 --> 00:00:08.908
Benjamin Franklin drew up a list of

4
00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:11.215
thirteen virtues he wanted to build.

5
00:00:11.215 --> 00:00:14.677
Chasing them all at once just scattered his attention.

6
00:00:15.927 --> 00:00:19.388
So he gave each virtue a full week of

7
00:00:19.388 --> 00:00:22.465
focus, and let the others take their chances.

8
00:00:22.465 --> 00:00:25.542
Every evening, a small black dot for each

9
00:00:25.542 --> 00:00:28.619
slip, aiming to keep that week's line clean.

10
00:00:29.869 --> 00:00:32.562
Thirteen weeks made a cycle, and he

11
00:00:32.562 --> 00:00:34.869
could run four cycles a year.

12
00:00:36.119 --> 00:00:38.812
Like weeding a garden, he worked on

13
00:00:38.812 --> 00:00:41.504
one of the beds at a time,

14
00:00:41.504 --> 00:00:44.196
not all the bad herbs at once.

15
00:00:45.446 --> 00:00:48.138
The same logic suits habit change today.

16
00:00:48.138 --> 00:00:51.215
Pick one behaviour, track it daily, and add

17
00:00:51.215 --> 00:00:54.292
the next only once the first feels automatic.

18
00:00:55.542 --> 00:00:58.619
Choose one habit to focus on this week.

19
00:00:58.619 --> 00:01:01.312
Draw seven boxes on a card, and

20
00:01:01.312 --> 00:01:04.004
add a dot each evening you slip.
